            <ArticleTitle>Coronary artery &quot;pseudothrombus&quot; due to collateral flow artifact distal to left circumflex coronary stenosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>425-9; discussion 429-30</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Since the complexity, morbidity, and costs of coronary interventions are increased when coronary thrombus is present, identification of the cause of an angiographic filling defect is potentially important. We present a case report and review our experience with a flow artifact that mimicked thrombus (&quot;pseudothrombus&quot;) in the setting of a severe proximal stenosis in the left circumflex coronary artery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
